{
  "contract": "lead.submitted.v1",
  "about": "Shared test vectors of the Traveller rules of lead.submitted.v1 (name, email, phone). One rule, applied the same way by the producer (AA-TripPlanner-Web backend/assembly/leads.py validate and frontend/lib/leadForm.ts) and the consumer (AA-Partner api/app/tripplanner/leads.py traveller_errors): control characters removed, Unicode NFC, trimmed, then the length in code points and the pattern. name: required, 1..120, and it must hold at least one name token: after the Unicode NFKD decomposition at least one character of category L (letter) or N (digit), pattern name_token_pattern; this is what the CRM's blind index (AA-Partner api/app/vault/blind_index.py name_tokens) needs to file the traveller, so a name of punctuation, symbols or emoji only ('-', '...', an em dash) is refused before storing, never stored and then lost at the agency. email: required, at most 254, pattern email_pattern, compared lower-case. phone: optional (null or empty = absent), at most 40, pattern phone_pattern (E.164 with its country code). The root file is the source; each app keeps a byte copy (TripPlanner backend/tests/contracts/, AA-Partner docs/contracts/rules/).",
  "control_characters": "[\\u0000-\\u0008\\u000b\\u000c\\u000e-\\u001f\\u007f]",
  "max_length": {
    "name": 120,
    "email": 254,
    "phone": 40
  },
  "name_token_normalisation": "NFKD",
  "name_token_pattern": "[\\p{L}\\p{N}]",
  "email_pattern": "^[^@\\s]{1,64}@[A-Za-z0-9-]+(\\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*\\.[A-Za-z]{2,63}$",
  "phone_pattern": "^\\+[1-9][0-9 ()-]{5,39}$",
